WEBVTT

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.999
Activate
the bio-temporal chamber.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.907
Is she going to be all right?

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.842
Not if you don't all
clear out of here

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.105
and let me do my work.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.737
She's my mother.
I'm staying.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.611
This is
a very delicate procedure

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.411
and I could use
some peace and quiet.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.384
The Doctor's right.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.886
Let's let him do his work.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.979
All right.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:37.394
I wish I'd told you this before
but better late than never.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.838
You're the finest friend
I've ever had.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:44.776
Prepare to bring the
bio-temporal chamber on line.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.006
We'll begin in approximately
five minutes.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.819
Grandma, are you awake?

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.256
I brought you a present.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.559
Grandma Kes?

00:02:59.377 --> 00:03:01.709
I finally finished making
your birthday present.

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:05.945
Sorry it's late,
but I wanted to get it right.

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:09.452
I... I don't know you.

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.115
What do you mean?

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:13.624
I'm Andrew...

00:03:13.658 --> 00:03:15.421
your grandson.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.960
I don't know you.

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:21.794
Doctor.
Dr. Van Gogh.

00:03:23.201 --> 00:03:24.361
What is it?

00:03:24.402 --> 00:03:26.336
She doesn't recognize me.

00:03:26.371 --> 00:03:28.362
Kes?

00:03:28.406 --> 00:03:30.499
How are you feeling?

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:31.509
Where am I?

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:32.771
What is this place?

00:03:34.646 --> 00:03:36.273
You're in Sick Bay.

00:03:36.314 --> 00:03:38.214
Do you know who I am?

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.649
No.

00:03:46.057 --> 00:03:47.547
Yes.

00:03:49.027 --> 00:03:51.495
I've seen you before.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.293
Do you know my name?

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.099
The boy, he called you
Dr. Van Gogh.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:01.967
That's right.

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:11.773
You said
I was your finest friend.

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:15.951
Well... I'm not sure
I've ever said that exactly,

00:04:15.987 --> 00:04:19.445
but... that doesn't mean
it's not true.

00:04:19.491 --> 00:04:21.891
How could I be your friend?

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.451
I don't know you.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.821
Tell me what you do remember.

00:04:30.268 --> 00:04:33.863
Uh, people around me,
crowded around me.

00:04:33.905 --> 00:04:36.738
You... a boy... a young girl.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.076
I was in a chamber...

00:04:43.381 --> 00:04:45.679
a bio-temporal chamber.

00:04:45.717 --> 00:04:46.979
Good.

00:04:47.085 --> 00:04:48.143
I was inside it

00:04:48.186 --> 00:04:50.620
and you told someone
to activate it.

00:04:52.224 --> 00:04:53.987
I'm afraid you're confused.

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:56.152
I discussed the bio-temporal
chamber with you,

00:04:56.194 --> 00:04:59.163
but we're not ready
to put you inside it just yet.

00:04:59.197 --> 00:05:03.759
Can you recall anything else
besides those people you saw?

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:05.565
Anything else about your life?

00:05:08.773 --> 00:05:10.638
No.

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:17.973
Go find the rest of your family.

00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:22.516
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:05:22.554 --> 00:05:23.851
What's the big hurry?

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:25.151
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:26.418
I have to go.

00:05:29.394 --> 00:05:30.361
What was that all about?

00:05:30.395 --> 00:05:32.295
I'm afraid Kes
is getting worse, Captain.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.958
Her amnesia is near total.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.865
Fewer than one percent
of her engrams

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:37.869
remained intact.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.495
It's as if her memory
were wiped clean.

00:05:39.537 --> 00:05:41.437
Is it some sort of senility?

00:05:41.473 --> 00:05:44.271
Maybe. I've never treated
a nine-year-old Ocampan before.

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:45.674
For all I know,

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:48.577
it's a perfectly normal part
of their aging process.

00:05:48.613 --> 00:05:49.580
It's hard to believe

00:05:49.614 --> 00:05:51.514
that she performed
microsurgery on my elbow

00:05:51.549 --> 00:05:52.743
just a few weeks ago.

00:05:52.784 --> 00:05:54.775
A few weeks ago,
she was a healthy woman,

00:05:54.819 --> 00:05:57.117
but this morilogium
comes on abruptly

00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:58.213
and then progresses

00:05:58.256 --> 00:06:00.417
with a rapidity
I've never seen before.

00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:03.427
How are you coming along
with the bio-temporal chamber?

00:06:03.461 --> 00:06:07.295
As I told you, it's a completely
revolutionary procedure.

00:06:07.332 --> 00:06:09.266
I have no idea if it'll work.

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:10.529
Under normal circumstances,

00:06:10.568 --> 00:06:13.833
I'd want to perform extensive
tests on the apparatus,

00:06:13.872 --> 00:06:15.499
but we're losing her too fast.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.508
If I don't try it now,
it may be too late.

00:06:17.542 --> 00:06:19.533
If you really believe
it will prolong her life...

00:06:19.577 --> 00:06:22.068
If we're lucky, it may
buy her another year.

00:06:22.113 --> 00:06:23.944
I think you have
the family's consent.

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:25.311
You should go ahead
and do it.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.408
I'm so cold.

00:06:30.622 --> 00:06:32.089
I'm cold.

00:06:32.123 --> 00:06:33.613
No wonder.

00:06:33.658 --> 00:06:35.489
Your temperature has dropped
to 14.8...

00:06:35.527 --> 00:06:37.119
almost two degrees below normal.

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:38.595
What does that mean?

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:39.790
I'm not sure.

00:06:39.831 --> 00:06:41.321
What?

00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:43.664
Her cells are in a state
of bio-temporal flux.

00:06:43.702 --> 00:06:45.636
I don't understand
how that could be happening

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.160
before I put her in the chamber.

00:06:47.205 --> 00:06:48.968
I'm cold.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:41.925
Look, Mom, I'm almost finished
with Grandma's present.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.450
It's wonderful, sweetheart.

00:07:43.495 --> 00:07:46.259
I'm sure Grandma will think
it was well worth the wait.

00:07:46.297 --> 00:07:48.197
I hope so.

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.257
I still feel bad

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.996
about not having it ready
in time for her party.

00:07:53.104 --> 00:07:54.901
Hello.

00:07:54.939 --> 00:07:55.997
How was your nap?

00:07:57.375 --> 00:07:58.467
Andrew?

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.477
Grandma, don't look.

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:01.445
You'll ruin the surprise.

00:08:01.479 --> 00:08:03.379
Why don't you sit down?

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:05.076
I'll get you some tea.

00:08:07.585 --> 00:08:09.678
Where am I?

00:08:09.721 --> 00:08:11.348
In your quarters.

00:08:11.389 --> 00:08:12.720
What quarters?

00:08:14.959 --> 00:08:16.824
Aboard Voyager.

00:08:16.861 --> 00:08:17.919
What's wrong?

00:08:17.962 --> 00:08:20.760
I don't know who you are.

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:25.702
But you...

00:08:25.737 --> 00:08:27.705
I know who you are.

00:08:29.207 --> 00:08:30.902
Tell me what's happening.

00:08:30.942 --> 00:08:32.534
How did I get here?

00:08:32.577 --> 00:08:34.511
Andrew, get your grandfather
and father.

00:08:34.546 --> 00:08:36.343
Tell them to meet us
in Sick Bay.

00:08:36.381 --> 00:08:39.942
Yes... Sick Bay.

00:08:39.984 --> 00:08:41.110
I remember that place.

00:08:41.152 --> 00:08:42.278
I was just there.

00:08:44.556 --> 00:08:46.217
Uh, when?

00:08:46.257 --> 00:08:49.090
Just a few minutes ago.

00:08:49.127 --> 00:08:53.655
Dr. Van Gogh
asked me some questions.

00:08:53.698 --> 00:08:57.395
I couldn't remember anything.

00:08:57.435 --> 00:09:02.202
You haven't been
to Sick Bay for over a week...

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.209
since you stopped working there.

00:09:05.243 --> 00:09:06.505
Working?

00:09:06.544 --> 00:09:07.568
What kind of work?

00:09:07.612 --> 00:09:08.579
Don't you remember?

00:09:08.613 --> 00:09:10.478
You were one
of the ship's doctors.

00:09:10.515 --> 00:09:11.880
I worked there with you.

00:09:13.351 --> 00:09:14.477
Who are you?

00:09:14.519 --> 00:09:18.546
I'm your daughter... Linnis.

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:22.685
But I don't remember you.

00:09:22.727 --> 00:09:25.252
Do you remember anything at all?

00:09:25.296 --> 00:09:28.891
Just people crowded around me...

00:09:28.933 --> 00:09:29.922
voices...

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.167
The Doctor told
everyone to leave

00:09:34.205 --> 00:09:35.797
and then he told someone else

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.604
to activate
the bio-temporal chamber.

00:09:38.643 --> 00:09:39.610
He's been working on that.

00:09:39.644 --> 00:09:40.872
He may have mentioned it to you.

00:09:40.912 --> 00:09:42.436
And then I woke up

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.710
and there was a boy...
Andrew...

00:09:44.749 --> 00:09:46.740
standing over me
with a present...

00:09:46.784 --> 00:09:49.184
calling me Grandma.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:51.950
But Andrew hasn't finished
your present yet.

00:09:52.023 --> 00:09:53.581
You just saw him
still working on it

00:09:53.625 --> 00:09:54.614
in your quarters.

00:09:55.627 --> 00:09:57.424
But he was there.

00:09:57.462 --> 00:10:00.795
The Doctor sent him
to get my family

00:10:00.832 --> 00:10:02.959
and I was cold and I woke up
in that bed

00:10:03.001 --> 00:10:03.968
in the quarters and...

00:10:04.002 --> 00:10:04.991
Maybe you were dreaming.

00:10:07.672 --> 00:10:10.937
I... I don't think so.

00:10:10.975 --> 00:10:13.239
Well, none of the things
that you remember

00:10:13.278 --> 00:10:15.337
before waking from your nap
have happened.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.109
How do you know?

00:10:17.148 --> 00:10:18.547
Listen to me, Mother.

00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:19.982
You're confused right now

00:10:20.084 --> 00:10:22.245
and I'm sure
that's very frightening.

00:10:22.287 --> 00:10:24.983
But you need to trust me.

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:27.082
I'm your daughter
and I love you.

00:10:27.125 --> 00:10:28.820
Now, please, come with me.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:30.088
Come.

00:10:33.331 --> 00:10:35.162
I've been expecting this.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.168
The onset of morilogium.

00:10:38.369 --> 00:10:41.634
She's lost more than 98 percent
of her memory engrams.

00:10:41.673 --> 00:10:43.368
Morilogium?

00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:47.174
The final phase of the Ocampan
life-span, Mother.

00:10:47.212 --> 00:10:49.737
Are you saying that I'm dying?

00:10:49.781 --> 00:10:51.510
Not if I can help it.

00:10:51.549 --> 00:10:53.244
What do you mean?

00:10:54.953 --> 00:10:58.184
Kes, it's me, Tom.

00:10:59.757 --> 00:11:01.588
Your husband.

00:11:02.961 --> 00:11:04.792
Tom.

00:11:04.829 --> 00:11:06.797
We're losing her.

00:11:08.666 --> 00:11:10.224
How long?

00:11:10.268 --> 00:11:12.793
If we do nothing,
a matter of weeks.

00:11:12.837 --> 00:11:15.772
But I'm working on something
to extend her life-span.

00:11:15.807 --> 00:11:18.139
It involves treating her
with a bio-temporal field

00:11:18.176 --> 00:11:19.837
in order to push her cells back

00:11:19.877 --> 00:11:21.970
to an earlier stage
of entropic decay.

00:11:22.013 --> 00:11:22.980
It's highly experimental,

00:11:23.014 --> 00:11:25.574
but if it works, it might
buy her some time.

00:11:25.617 --> 00:11:27.414
No.
My mother's always accepted

00:11:27.452 --> 00:11:29.511
that she would
only live nine years.

00:11:29.554 --> 00:11:31.181
If she's reaching
the natural end of her life,

00:11:31.222 --> 00:11:34.157
she wouldn't want extraordinary
measures taken to extend it.

00:11:34.192 --> 00:11:35.989
Especially not in the state
she's in now.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:37.925
If the Doctor has a way
to keep your mother with us,

00:11:37.962 --> 00:11:40.089
even for one more day,
we have to let him try.

00:11:40.131 --> 00:11:42.622
We're not talking about
a tested medical procedure here.

00:11:42.667 --> 00:11:44.294
We're talking
about a radical experiment.

00:11:44.335 --> 00:11:47.202
Sweetheart, I understand
how upsetting this is.

00:11:47.238 --> 00:11:49.001
But if it were you
on that bio-bed,

00:11:49.107 --> 00:11:50.836
I'd feel just like Tom does.

00:11:50.875 --> 00:11:53.105
Everyone, listen to me, please.

00:11:53.144 --> 00:11:54.634
Yes, listen to her.

00:11:54.679 --> 00:11:56.909
Mother, tell us what you want.

00:11:56.948 --> 00:11:58.176
I want to know
what's going on here.

00:11:58.216 --> 00:12:00.013
Maybe the morilogium
is causing my amnesia,

00:12:00.118 --> 00:12:01.415
but that doesn't explain

00:12:01.452 --> 00:12:04.546
how I seem to suddenly jump
from Sick Bay to my quarters,

00:12:04.589 --> 00:12:08.958
or how I remember being
in a bio-temporal chamber.

00:12:08.993 --> 00:12:10.392
Kes, it's possible
the morilogium

00:12:10.428 --> 00:12:12.123
is causing you
to experience delusions.

00:12:12.163 --> 00:12:13.528
No, they're not delusions!

00:12:13.564 --> 00:12:14.531
I want you to lie down.

00:12:14.565 --> 00:12:15.532
No.

00:12:15.566 --> 00:12:16.624
Leave her alone.

00:12:16.668 --> 00:12:18.067
Your grandmother's very sick,
son.

00:12:18.102 --> 00:12:20.070
Maybe, but she's not delusional.

00:12:20.104 --> 00:12:21.935
She's the smartest person
I know.

00:12:21.973 --> 00:12:23.167
We should listen to her.

00:12:23.207 --> 00:12:25.471
Oh, I'm cold.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:32.177
Her body temperature
has dropped 2.7 degrees.

00:12:32.216 --> 00:12:35.185
...For she's
a jolly good fellow

00:12:35.219 --> 00:12:37.983
For she's a jolly good fellow

00:12:38.022 --> 00:12:42.755
For she's
a jolly good fellow

00:12:42.794 --> 00:12:45.786
Which nobody can deny.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.821
Happy ninth, Kes.

00:12:47.865 --> 00:12:48.923
Well, go ahead.

00:12:48.966 --> 00:12:50.524
Make a wish.

00:12:56.841 --> 00:12:58.103
Well, what are you waiting for?

00:12:58.142 --> 00:12:59.131
Blow out the candles.

00:13:04.615 --> 00:13:07.709
It's good to see that old lung
is still working, Kessy.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.583
Happy birthday, sweetheart.

00:13:14.158 --> 00:13:16.626
Why, you know, I haven't
made one of these

00:13:16.661 --> 00:13:19.425
since... well, since I
became Security Officer.

00:13:19.464 --> 00:13:21.432
Perhaps you would care
to relinquish your commission

00:13:21.466 --> 00:13:24.435
and return to the scene
of your former triumphs.

00:13:24.469 --> 00:13:25.436
You keep working

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:27.961
on that sense of humor,
Commander Vulcan.

00:13:28.005 --> 00:13:30.303
You'll get it one of these days.

00:13:32.343 --> 00:13:33.810
Jimbalian fudge... your favorite.

00:13:33.845 --> 00:13:35.813
Some of us ought to be
watching our calories,

00:13:35.847 --> 00:13:38.281
but after all, it is
a special occasion.

00:13:39.384 --> 00:13:40.510
Andrew.

00:13:43.855 --> 00:13:46.187
I'm sorry I don't have a
present for you, Grandma.

00:13:46.224 --> 00:13:48.920
I've got an idea
for something special

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.450
I'm going to make,
but I've been

00:13:50.495 --> 00:13:51.655
too busy with schoolwork.

00:13:51.696 --> 00:13:52.856
I haven't had a chance
to start it.

00:13:52.897 --> 00:13:55.331
I think it'll be worth the wait.

00:13:55.366 --> 00:13:57.095
Come and talk to Grandma
for a minute, will you?

00:13:57.135 --> 00:13:58.102
Sure.

00:13:58.136 --> 00:13:59.694
I'm going to ask
you a few questions

00:13:59.737 --> 00:14:01.034
and I want you
to think very carefully

00:14:01.072 --> 00:14:03.063
before you answer them,
all right?

00:14:03.107 --> 00:14:04.938
I always think before I speak.

00:14:05.009 --> 00:14:06.374
You taught me that.

00:14:06.411 --> 00:14:09.744
Where were you before you
came to this party?

00:14:09.781 --> 00:14:12.341
At my physics lesson
in Engineering.

00:14:12.383 --> 00:14:14.647
And then you came directly here?

00:14:14.685 --> 00:14:16.812
No. I stopped at your quarters
to get you.

00:14:16.854 --> 00:14:18.378
Don't you remember?

00:14:18.423 --> 00:14:20.482
Andrew, stop monopolizing
your grandmother's time.

00:14:20.525 --> 00:14:22.459
There are other people
who'd would like to wish her

00:14:22.493 --> 00:14:23.517
a happy birthday, you know.

00:14:23.561 --> 00:14:25.552
She's all yours, Doctor.

00:14:25.596 --> 00:14:28.533
Excuse me.
That cake looks great.

00:14:28.666 --> 00:14:30.224
It's amazing to think

00:14:30.268 --> 00:14:32.964
that you weren't even a year old
when we first met.

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:34.594
Not much older than Andrew.

00:14:34.639 --> 00:14:37.073
Doctor, there's
something wrong with me.

00:14:37.108 --> 00:14:38.234
What is it?

00:14:38.276 --> 00:14:41.074
Promise to hear me out
and not assume I'm delusional.

00:14:41.112 --> 00:14:43.171
Why do you think I'd ever
make such an assumption?

00:14:43.214 --> 00:14:44.203
Promise.

00:14:44.248 --> 00:14:45.272
Of course.

00:14:45.316 --> 00:14:46.977
I've lost all
but a few of my memories

00:14:47.084 --> 00:14:48.278
and the memories I do have

00:14:48.319 --> 00:14:49.877
don't coincide
with anyone else's.

00:14:49.921 --> 00:14:51.980
Can you be more specific?

00:14:52.023 --> 00:14:54.491
Well, I was in Sick Bay

00:14:54.525 --> 00:14:57.756
and you and a woman,
my daughter,

00:14:57.795 --> 00:15:02.061
were arguing
about prolonging my life

00:15:02.099 --> 00:15:03.930
and then I suddenly
appeared in my quarters

00:15:04.035 --> 00:15:05.559
and then I simply appeared here.

00:15:05.603 --> 00:15:07.833
As far as I know,
none of that happened.

00:15:07.872 --> 00:15:09.737
Is it possible
you were dreaming?

00:15:09.774 --> 00:15:11.935
No. I was awake.
I'm sure of it.

00:15:12.043 --> 00:15:14.238
But nobody else remembers
the things I do.

00:15:14.278 --> 00:15:17.736
I hate to say this,
but... it's possible

00:15:17.782 --> 00:15:20.342
that these strange
experiences you're having

00:15:20.384 --> 00:15:22.944
are related to the onset
of the morilogium.

00:15:22.987 --> 00:15:24.579
You talked about that.

00:15:24.622 --> 00:15:25.816
You wanted to put me

00:15:25.856 --> 00:15:28.950
in a bio-temporal chamber
to stop my aging process.

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:30.857
How could you possibly
know about that?

00:15:30.895 --> 00:15:32.624
Because you told me.

00:15:32.663 --> 00:15:33.960
I only came up with the idea

00:15:33.998 --> 00:15:36.432
for the bio-temporal
chamber this morning.

00:15:36.467 --> 00:15:37.957
I was going to tell you
about it today,

00:15:38.069 --> 00:15:40.970
here, at the party
as a sort of birthday surprise.

00:15:41.005 --> 00:15:41.972
If that were true,

00:15:42.006 --> 00:15:43.405
then how could I
already know about it?

00:15:44.575 --> 00:15:47.476
I don't know,
but we'd better get you

00:15:47.511 --> 00:15:49.274
to Sick Bay and find out.

00:15:49.313 --> 00:15:52.077
She appears to have lost
more than 95 percent

00:15:52.116 --> 00:15:53.981
of her memory engrams.

00:15:54.085 --> 00:15:56.076
Is that symptomatic
of the morilogium?

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:57.087
I don't know.

00:15:57.121 --> 00:15:58.588
I have no basis for comparison.

00:15:58.623 --> 00:16:00.284
No other Ocampans on board.

00:16:00.324 --> 00:16:02.087
Don't worry.

00:16:02.126 --> 00:16:03.650
We'll get to the bottom of this.

00:16:03.694 --> 00:16:04.661
I do have memories.

00:16:04.695 --> 00:16:06.424
They just don't coincide
with anyone else's.

00:16:06.464 --> 00:16:08.591
First, Andrew gave me
a belated birthday present.

00:16:08.633 --> 00:16:10.533
Then, he said he
was working on the present.

00:16:10.568 --> 00:16:13.662
And now he just apologized
for not starting it yet.

00:16:13.704 --> 00:16:16.138
It's almost as if
you're experiencing

00:16:16.173 --> 00:16:17.367
events in reverse.

00:16:17.408 --> 00:16:20.275
Maybe there's some kind
of time paradox at work.

00:16:20.311 --> 00:16:22.142
There is another possibility.

00:16:22.179 --> 00:16:23.271
Given that Kes has knowledge

00:16:23.314 --> 00:16:26.044
of a treatment I have not
yet devised, it's possible

00:16:26.083 --> 00:16:28.278
she's developed some
sort of precognition.

00:16:28.319 --> 00:16:30.753
Are you saying I can see
into the future?

00:16:30.788 --> 00:16:32.221
Well, you've demonstrated some

00:16:32.256 --> 00:16:33.951
pretty extraordinary
mental powers

00:16:33.991 --> 00:16:36.585
over the years...
telepathy, telekinesis.

00:16:36.627 --> 00:16:39.255
And precognition wouldn't be
unprecedented.

00:16:39.296 --> 00:16:41.856
Some species, including the
Yattho of the Beta Quadrant,

00:16:41.899 --> 00:16:43.662
have been known to predict
future events

00:16:43.701 --> 00:16:44.827
with uncanny accuracy.

00:16:44.869 --> 00:16:47.269
See if you can confirm this
theory about precognition.

00:16:47.304 --> 00:16:48.328
In the meantime, Tom and I

00:16:48.372 --> 00:16:50.704
will begin scanning for temporal
anomalies.

00:16:50.741 --> 00:16:52.868
We'll do everything
we can to help you.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.707
I'd like to do something
to help myself.

00:16:54.745 --> 00:16:55.973
What did you have in mind?

00:16:56.013 --> 00:16:58.208
Well, I seem to have lived
quite a full life on this ship.

00:16:58.249 --> 00:16:59.807
Maybe if I had a look
at my medical files

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:01.818
or checked other records
of my activities,

00:17:01.852 --> 00:17:04.116
I might be able
to fill in some of the blanks.

00:17:04.155 --> 00:17:06.146
Well, you may have lost
your memories,

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.351
but you certainly haven't
lost your determination.

00:17:24.542 --> 00:17:25.736
Hi.

00:17:25.776 --> 00:17:27.801
Oh, hello.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.447
How's it coming?

00:17:30.481 --> 00:17:31.709
I've had a busy life.

00:17:31.749 --> 00:17:33.649
It's hard to know
where to start.

00:17:33.684 --> 00:17:35.618
How about you?

00:17:35.653 --> 00:17:37.780
Well, we've tried
every kind of temporal scan

00:17:37.822 --> 00:17:39.187
Harry could think of,

00:17:39.223 --> 00:17:40.952
but we still haven't
been able to find anything

00:17:41.058 --> 00:17:43.049
to explain what's
been happening to you.

00:17:45.663 --> 00:17:48.131
Your initial physical exam.

00:17:48.165 --> 00:17:50.429
I remember
when you came on board.

00:17:50.468 --> 00:17:52.834
I had a crush on you
right from the beginning.

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:55.134
I tried to hide it,
but Neelix sensed it

00:17:55.172 --> 00:17:57.402
and, boy, was he ever jealous.

00:17:57.441 --> 00:17:58.965
Neelix?

00:17:59.076 --> 00:18:01.067
You don't remember?

00:18:02.213 --> 00:18:05.808
You and he were
involved for quite a while.

00:18:07.752 --> 00:18:09.777
Oh, one of your prenatal exams.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:11.913
When we listened
to Linnis's heartbeat.

00:18:11.956 --> 00:18:14.356
That was quite a day.

00:18:16.894 --> 00:18:18.088
What about this?

00:18:18.129 --> 00:18:20.063
It says I got some kind
of radiation poisoning

00:18:20.097 --> 00:18:24.056
on stardate 50973.

00:18:24.101 --> 00:18:28.561
That was the beginning
of the Year of Hell.

00:18:28.606 --> 00:18:29.698
"Year of Hell"?

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:32.436
Well, that's what some of us
call it now.

00:18:32.476 --> 00:18:34.706
We were
under virtually constant attack

00:18:34.745 --> 00:18:36.474
by a race called the Krenim.

00:18:36.514 --> 00:18:38.482
The ship almost didn't make it.

00:18:38.516 --> 00:18:40.643
The Doctor was off-line
for months,

00:18:40.684 --> 00:18:42.174
and we lost
a lot of good people...

00:18:42.219 --> 00:18:46.849
Captain Janeway,
Joe Carey... B'Elanna.

00:18:48.359 --> 00:18:50.054
B'Elanna?

00:18:52.596 --> 00:18:55.429
I keep forgetting that you
don't remember any of them.

00:18:58.035 --> 00:19:04.031
B'Elanna was... someone
who was very special to me.

00:19:04.074 --> 00:19:10.070
When she died, I felt like I
wanted to die, too.

00:19:11.682 --> 00:19:13.912
But you...

00:19:13.951 --> 00:19:16.146
you helped me through it.

00:19:16.187 --> 00:19:17.586
I'm sorry.

00:19:17.621 --> 00:19:19.111
No.

00:19:19.156 --> 00:19:20.214
No. It's my fault.

00:19:20.257 --> 00:19:22.191
You haven't done anything wrong.

00:19:22.226 --> 00:19:23.921
It's just...

00:19:24.028 --> 00:19:25.962
You don't remember
any of our life together?

00:19:30.067 --> 00:19:31.295
Well, that's all right.

00:19:31.335 --> 00:19:35.635
I've got enough feelings
for both of us.

00:19:35.673 --> 00:19:39.302
Maybe the feelings
I had for you will come back.

00:19:44.882 --> 00:19:47.476
You were asking
about the radiation poisoning.

00:19:47.518 --> 00:19:48.917
A lot of us were exposed.

00:19:48.953 --> 00:19:50.944
During the first Krenim attack,

00:19:50.988 --> 00:19:52.421
one of the chroniton
torpedo fragments

00:19:52.456 --> 00:19:54.321
leaked radiation into the ship.

00:19:56.293 --> 00:19:57.419
Chroniton torpedoes?

00:19:57.461 --> 00:19:59.452
They were able
to penetrate our shields

00:19:59.496 --> 00:20:00.463
because their torpedoes

00:20:00.497 --> 00:20:02.362
were in a constant state
of temporal flux.

00:20:04.168 --> 00:20:05.157
Wait a minute.

00:20:06.437 --> 00:20:08.962
I think we may be
onto something.

00:20:09.073 --> 00:20:11.064
We'd better go talk
to the Doctor.

00:20:11.108 --> 00:20:13.167
Come on.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:15.144
If I was infected with
these chroniton particles,

00:20:15.179 --> 00:20:17.443
there might be a connection
to what's happening to me now.

00:20:17.481 --> 00:20:18.470
Exactly.

00:20:18.515 --> 00:20:20.278
Maybe we should try
scanning for residual...

00:20:22.753 --> 00:20:24.721
Say cheese.

00:20:27.091 --> 00:20:28.285
Oh...

00:20:31.896 --> 00:20:35.923
I think he's got
your nose, Mother.

00:20:35.966 --> 00:20:38.867
So how does it feel
to be a grandfather?

00:20:38.903 --> 00:20:41.463
A lot better than it does
to have you for a son-in-law.

00:20:42.907 --> 00:20:44.898
What's the date?

00:20:44.942 --> 00:20:46.341
The date?

00:20:46.377 --> 00:20:47.844
Yes. The stardate.

00:20:49.446 --> 00:20:51.277
It's 56947. Why?

00:20:52.516 --> 00:20:53.915
Over six months.

00:20:53.951 --> 00:20:55.145
Mother, what's going on?

00:21:00.391 --> 00:21:01.949
Tom, we have to talk
to the Doctor.

00:21:01.992 --> 00:21:02.981
Come on.

00:21:05.462 --> 00:21:07.054
As far as I can tell,
I've jumped backwards

00:21:07.097 --> 00:21:08.792
a total of five times so far.

00:21:08.832 --> 00:21:11.232
Is there any discernible
pattern to these jumps?

00:21:11.268 --> 00:21:13.202
No. They're apparently random.

00:21:13.237 --> 00:21:15.865
Uh, one time it seemed
to span for a few weeks

00:21:15.906 --> 00:21:17.897
and the last was half a year.

00:21:17.942 --> 00:21:20.672
Each time I arrive, I seem
to exist in temporal sync

00:21:20.711 --> 00:21:22.144
with the rest of you
for a while,

00:21:22.179 --> 00:21:24.545
but before I can make anyone
understand what's happening,

00:21:24.581 --> 00:21:27.379
I find myself
at an earlier time in my life

00:21:27.418 --> 00:21:29.545
and just before it happens,
I seem to experience

00:21:29.586 --> 00:21:31.554
a sudden drop
in body temperature.

00:21:32.923 --> 00:21:33.890
Hmm.

00:21:33.924 --> 00:21:36.188
Now, this could explain
a thing or two.

00:21:36.226 --> 00:21:37.193
What is it?

00:21:37.227 --> 00:21:39.388
I'm detecting high-level
chroniton radiation

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:40.397
in your cells.

00:21:40.431 --> 00:21:42.490
So I was right.

00:21:42.533 --> 00:21:43.591
There is a connection.

00:21:43.634 --> 00:21:45.829
But Kes was inoculated
along with the rest of the crew

00:21:45.869 --> 00:21:46.995
over three years ago.

00:21:47.037 --> 00:21:48.800
Yes, however, everyone was left

00:21:48.839 --> 00:21:51.467
with trace amounts of the
radiation in their bodies.

00:21:51.508 --> 00:21:54.477
For some reason,
those residual chronitons

00:21:54.511 --> 00:21:55.944
have reactivated in Kes.

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:56.947
Why?

00:21:56.981 --> 00:21:58.005
The bio-temporal chamber.

00:21:58.115 --> 00:21:59.707
My thinking exactly.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.684
Would you two mind explaining?

00:22:01.719 --> 00:22:03.414
It's really quite obvious,
Lieutenant.

00:22:03.454 --> 00:22:06.446
Your wife is traveling
backward through time.

00:22:15.733 --> 00:22:17.291
It's as though
I came into existence

00:22:17.334 --> 00:22:20.303
at the moment of my own death
without any memories.

00:22:20.337 --> 00:22:22.669
I've been living my life
backwards ever since...

00:22:22.706 --> 00:22:25.539
jumping progressively
to earlier moments in my life,

00:22:25.576 --> 00:22:29.376
accumulating memories
and experiences as I go.

00:22:29.413 --> 00:22:31.847
Your past has become my future.

00:22:31.882 --> 00:22:34.783
Doctor, any theory
about what's causing this?

00:22:34.818 --> 00:22:38.584
In approximately six months,
I will apparently expose Kes

00:22:38.622 --> 00:22:40.487
to some type
of bio-temporal field

00:22:40.524 --> 00:22:43.550
in a highly experimental, but
nonetheless brilliant attempt

00:22:43.594 --> 00:22:45.152
to stop her aging process.

00:22:45.195 --> 00:22:46.389
And it's this attempt

00:22:46.430 --> 00:22:48.489
which leads
to Kes's current predicament?

00:22:48.532 --> 00:22:51.000
What I will, apparently,
fail to realize

00:22:51.035 --> 00:22:53.469
is that the bio-temporal field
is going to reactivate

00:22:53.504 --> 00:22:55.836
the dormant chroniton particles
in her cells,

00:22:55.873 --> 00:22:58.774
bringing Kes out of temporal
sync with the rest of us.

00:22:58.809 --> 00:23:01.676
Is there any way to stop Kes
from continuing these jumps?

00:23:01.712 --> 00:23:04.146
Yes. Purge her completely
of the chroniton poisoning.

00:23:04.181 --> 00:23:07.082
To do that, we'd need to know
the precise temporal variance

00:23:07.117 --> 00:23:09.677
of the specific torpedo
which contaminated the ship.

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:12.314
Tactical sensors were not
functioning at the time.

00:23:12.356 --> 00:23:15.519
There is no data regarding
the torpedo in question.

00:23:15.559 --> 00:23:17.686
Let me get one thing straight,
Doc.

00:23:17.728 --> 00:23:19.821
Is it possible, if this
keeps happening to Kes,

00:23:19.863 --> 00:23:22.354
that she might actually
jump back into a time

00:23:22.399 --> 00:23:23.957
before she knew any of us?

00:23:24.001 --> 00:23:25.559
Worse than that, Mr. Paris.

00:23:25.602 --> 00:23:27.433
It's possible she may
eventually jump back

00:23:27.471 --> 00:23:30.929
to a time...
before she even existed.

00:23:38.015 --> 00:23:41.382
Captain's Log, Stardate 55836.2.

00:23:41.418 --> 00:23:43.648
Kes has remained
in temporal sync with us

00:23:43.687 --> 00:23:44.984
for two days now,

00:23:45.022 --> 00:23:46.922
but since we don't know
when she may jump again,

00:23:46.957 --> 00:23:47.981
we can't afford to rest

00:23:48.025 --> 00:23:49.822
until we've found some way
to help her.

00:23:50.994 --> 00:23:53.326
I'm going to try running
a hypothalamic scan.

00:23:53.363 --> 00:23:55.558
Maybe we can establish a pattern

00:23:55.599 --> 00:23:57.362
to the drops
in your body temperature.

00:23:57.401 --> 00:23:58.868
You're very good at this,
aren't you?

00:23:58.902 --> 00:24:01.097
I had a very good teacher.

00:24:01.138 --> 00:24:02.833
Doctor van Gogh?

00:24:02.873 --> 00:24:04.306
You.

00:24:04.341 --> 00:24:06.673
I'm sorry.
All this must be taking you

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:08.473
away from your baby just now.

00:24:08.512 --> 00:24:11.481
You must be wanting to spend
every second with him.

00:24:12.683 --> 00:24:15.777
Actually, I feel a little
awkward around him sometimes.

00:24:15.819 --> 00:24:21.553
Harry's always singing to him
and playing with him, but...

00:24:21.592 --> 00:24:23.890
Well, I seem to be
much more comfortable

00:24:23.927 --> 00:24:26.828
with a molecular scanner
than I am with a diaper.

00:24:26.864 --> 00:24:28.957
Oh, Linnis,
I don't think that...

00:24:28.999 --> 00:24:30.864
Kes, I may have found a way
to prevent your next jump.

00:24:30.901 --> 00:24:33.062
I've erected a containment field
that may keep you here.

00:24:33.103 --> 00:24:34.866
It's going to require
your confinement in Sick Bay.

00:24:34.905 --> 00:24:36.065
I'll keep working here.

00:24:36.106 --> 00:24:40.236
Linnis... you must
be a good mother.

00:24:40.277 --> 00:24:42.268
I happen to know
that Andrew grows up

00:24:42.312 --> 00:24:43.677
to be a wonderful child.

00:24:58.328 --> 00:24:59.818
Hello, Tom.

00:24:59.863 --> 00:25:02.559
I thought... maybe you
could use some company.

00:25:02.599 --> 00:25:04.362
I feel like I'm in a cage.

00:25:04.401 --> 00:25:05.766
Dr. Van Gogh says...

00:25:05.802 --> 00:25:07.394
Dr. "van Gogh"?

00:25:07.437 --> 00:25:09.371
I thought you
settled on "Mozart."

00:25:09.406 --> 00:25:11.067
Evidently, my interest

00:25:11.108 --> 00:25:12.837
in the great figures
of art and culture

00:25:12.876 --> 00:25:14.673
will be an ongoing process.

00:25:14.711 --> 00:25:17.111
Well...

00:25:17.147 --> 00:25:18.614
"Vincent"...uh...

00:25:18.649 --> 00:25:20.617
how about letting me
inside this thing?

00:25:20.651 --> 00:25:22.175
I'm afraid that wouldn't
be advisable.

00:25:25.455 --> 00:25:27.946
Okay, then...

00:25:27.991 --> 00:25:32.428
How about another installment
of Tom and Kes: The Early Years?

00:25:32.462 --> 00:25:34.760
I'd enjoy that.

00:25:34.798 --> 00:25:39.531
Um... well, there was,
uh, our wedding reception.

00:25:39.570 --> 00:25:41.970
Harry was my best man.

00:25:42.072 --> 00:25:43.505
He... he got so nervous

00:25:43.540 --> 00:25:44.871
when he stood up
to give the toast

00:25:44.908 --> 00:25:47.900
that he spilled champagne
all over my dress uniform.

00:25:50.478 --> 00:25:51.843
What is it?

00:25:53.481 --> 00:25:58.680
At the time, I thought that was
the happiest day of my life...

00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:02.816
but every day
just got better and better.

00:26:02.857 --> 00:26:05.451
It means so much
to have you here now.

00:26:09.197 --> 00:26:10.687
I think I may have
found something.

00:26:10.732 --> 00:26:11.699
What is it?

00:26:11.733 --> 00:26:12.757
Well, I was studying the effects

00:26:12.800 --> 00:26:14.427
of the chronitons on
other crew members and I...

00:26:15.470 --> 00:26:16.459
What's that?

00:26:17.472 --> 00:26:20.498
Kes' temperature
has dropped 1.9 degrees.

00:26:20.541 --> 00:26:21.940
Linnis, monitor
the containment field.

00:26:21.976 --> 00:26:23.500
I'm going to try to elevate
her temperature.

00:26:37.658 --> 00:26:38.920
Her temperature's
still dropping.

00:26:38.960 --> 00:26:40.427
We're losing containment.

00:26:40.461 --> 00:26:42.258
Increase the field amplitude.

00:26:42.296 --> 00:26:43.354
Kes?

00:26:43.398 --> 00:26:44.626
It's not working.

00:26:44.665 --> 00:26:45.632
We're losing her.

00:26:45.666 --> 00:26:47.531
Set field polarization
to maximum.

00:27:01.516 --> 00:27:03.711
Do something!

00:27:05.119 --> 00:27:06.916
The sac is opening...

00:27:07.021 --> 00:27:08.318
What's happening?

00:27:08.356 --> 00:27:09.584
What do you mean
"what's happening?"

00:27:09.624 --> 00:27:10.591
You're having a baby.

00:27:10.625 --> 00:27:11.592
Now, hold still.

00:27:11.626 --> 00:27:12.650
Where am I?

00:27:12.693 --> 00:27:14.627
Exactly where I told you
not to be...

00:27:14.662 --> 00:27:15.651
on a shuttlecraft.

00:27:15.696 --> 00:27:17.789
I have to see the Doctor.

00:27:17.832 --> 00:27:20.130
Well, that'd be nice
if he were still around.

00:27:21.035 --> 00:27:22.468
I told you,
you were in no condition

00:27:22.503 --> 00:27:24.630
to come on a supply mission,
but did you listen to me?

00:27:28.075 --> 00:27:29.838
I can see the toes...

00:27:30.878 --> 00:27:32.072
It's coming...

00:27:33.381 --> 00:27:36.043
Kes...

00:27:37.518 --> 00:27:39.543
Oh, it's a girl.

00:27:42.290 --> 00:27:44.758
Oh...

00:27:44.792 --> 00:27:46.316
Linnis.

00:27:46.360 --> 00:27:47.588
Shh...

00:27:47.628 --> 00:27:49.289
She's beautiful.

00:27:50.465 --> 00:27:51.591
Yes, she is.

00:27:51.632 --> 00:27:55.227
Yes, just like her mother.

00:27:55.269 --> 00:27:57.203
Tom...

00:27:57.238 --> 00:27:59.866
listen...

00:27:59.907 --> 00:28:03.035
I love you, Kes.

00:28:03.077 --> 00:28:05.671
We need to talk.

00:28:07.181 --> 00:28:08.443
Just a minute.

00:28:08.483 --> 00:28:09.677
But...

00:28:12.053 --> 00:28:13.918
What is it?

00:28:13.988 --> 00:28:16.456
Voyager's under attack.

00:28:25.700 --> 00:28:26.928
Congratulations.

00:28:26.968 --> 00:28:28.026
Thanks.

00:28:28.069 --> 00:28:30.537
But it looks like the
celebration'll have to wait.

00:28:31.806 --> 00:28:34.036
I'll get Kes and the baby
to the Mess Hall.

00:28:34.075 --> 00:28:36.339
Captain Chakotay wants you
to go to the weapons array

00:28:36.377 --> 00:28:38.072
and modulate
the targeting scanners

00:28:38.112 --> 00:28:40.637
to a parametric frequency.

00:28:40.681 --> 00:28:41.739
He's going to try to knock out

00:28:41.782 --> 00:28:43.909
the chroniton torpedo launchers
before they're fired.

00:28:43.951 --> 00:28:45.714
Chroniton torpedoes...
the "Year of Hell."

00:28:45.753 --> 00:28:46.777
What?

00:28:46.821 --> 00:28:48.379
You told me that the crew
referred to this time

00:28:48.422 --> 00:28:49.389
as the "Year of Hell."

00:28:49.423 --> 00:28:50.549
When did I tell you that?

00:28:50.591 --> 00:28:51.558
It's a long story.

00:28:53.327 --> 00:28:54.658
You'll have to tell me later.

00:28:54.695 --> 00:28:55.957
I've got to get
to the weapons array.

00:28:55.997 --> 00:28:57.794
Neelix, get her to lie down,
will you?

00:28:57.832 --> 00:28:59.459
Neelix, listen very carefully.

00:28:59.500 --> 00:29:01.331
There's something important
I have to tell you.

00:29:11.445 --> 00:29:13.777
Neelix told us what's been
happening to you, Kes.

00:29:13.814 --> 00:29:15.338
How are you holding up?

00:29:15.383 --> 00:29:16.372
We're both fine.

00:29:16.417 --> 00:29:17.884
It's quite a story.

00:29:17.919 --> 00:29:20.547
Just before the last jump,
we were close to a solution.

00:29:20.588 --> 00:29:21.555
The Doctor was working on...

00:29:21.589 --> 00:29:22.681
The Doctor?

00:29:22.723 --> 00:29:23.690
Well, it's good to know

00:29:23.724 --> 00:29:25.248
we'll eventually
get him back on line.

00:29:25.293 --> 00:29:26.760
"Eventually" may be too late.

00:29:26.794 --> 00:29:28.159
We've got to help Kes now.

00:29:28.195 --> 00:29:29.856
We discovered that what's
been happening to me

00:29:29.897 --> 00:29:31.262
is related
to the chroniton poisoning

00:29:31.299 --> 00:29:33.529
I suffered during
a Krenim attack.

00:29:33.568 --> 00:29:35.331
We have to determine
the exact temporal variance

00:29:35.369 --> 00:29:36.700
of the torpedo, so that we...

00:29:36.737 --> 00:29:39.433
The main computer's been
off-line for weeks.

00:29:39.473 --> 00:29:41.566
Even if the sensor logs
contain that information,

00:29:41.609 --> 00:29:42.598
we can't access them.

00:29:44.912 --> 00:29:46.880
You have to put me in the bio-
temporal containment field.

00:29:46.914 --> 00:29:49.382
I know it didn't work last time,
but with a few modifications...

00:29:49.417 --> 00:29:51.442
We've only got life-support
on three out of 14 decks.

00:29:51.485 --> 00:29:53.316
And we've had to divert
all remaining power

00:29:53.354 --> 00:29:55.618
to knock out the Krenim's
torpedo launchers.

00:29:55.656 --> 00:29:57.214
We don't even have
a Sick Bay anymore,

00:29:57.258 --> 00:29:58.452
much less the resources

00:29:58.492 --> 00:30:00.357
to create
a bio-containment field.

00:30:00.394 --> 00:30:01.588
I'm sorry.

00:30:01.629 --> 00:30:03.597
We've got to do
something to help her.

00:30:03.631 --> 00:30:04.757
I'm open to suggestions.

00:30:04.799 --> 00:30:06.460
I'm cold.

00:30:06.500 --> 00:30:07.467
I'll get you a blanket.

00:30:07.501 --> 00:30:09.662
No. You don't understand.

00:30:09.704 --> 00:30:10.932
I'm abou...

00:30:10.972 --> 00:30:11.939
I'm about...

00:30:20.982 --> 00:30:22.279
Tom...

00:30:22.316 --> 00:30:23.613
Hey, Kes.

00:30:23.651 --> 00:30:24.811
Some party, huh?

00:30:24.852 --> 00:30:26.513
I have to talk to you.

00:30:26.554 --> 00:30:27.521
Tom...

00:30:27.555 --> 00:30:28.852
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:30:32.627 --> 00:30:34.788
You must be B'Elanna.

00:30:37.531 --> 00:30:39.226
Well, the last time I checked.

00:30:39.266 --> 00:30:40.460
Is something wrong?

00:30:40.501 --> 00:30:42.093
Actually...

00:30:42.136 --> 00:30:43.364
there is something wrong.

00:30:44.405 --> 00:30:45.895
Red Alert.

00:30:45.940 --> 00:30:47.271
All hands to battle stations.

00:30:55.216 --> 00:30:56.183
Tuvok, fire phasers.

00:30:56.217 --> 00:30:57.149
Acknowledged.

00:31:01.656 --> 00:31:03.556
Who the hell are they?

00:31:03.591 --> 00:31:05.081
They're called the Krenim.

00:31:05.126 --> 00:31:06.093
How do you know that?

00:31:06.127 --> 00:31:07.094
Captain Janeway?

00:31:07.128 --> 00:31:08.095
What is it, Kes?

00:31:08.129 --> 00:31:09.687
What do you know about them?

00:31:09.730 --> 00:31:12.824
Shields down to 39 percent,
Captain.

00:31:12.867 --> 00:31:14.198
I don't understand
how these torpedoes

00:31:14.235 --> 00:31:15.532
are ripping right
through our shields.

00:31:15.569 --> 00:31:16.729
Evasive maneuvers, Mr. Paris.

00:31:16.771 --> 00:31:18.966
B'Elanna, can we reroute
power to the forward shields?

00:31:19.040 --> 00:31:20.166
I'm already trying.

00:31:20.207 --> 00:31:21.970
Captain, these torpedoes
are chroniton-based.

00:31:22.043 --> 00:31:23.340
They're passing through
our shields

00:31:23.377 --> 00:31:25.072
because they're in a state
of temporal flux.

00:31:43.097 --> 00:31:44.428
They're dead.

00:31:55.409 --> 00:31:56.967
B'Elanna!

00:31:59.246 --> 00:32:00.907
Hull breach on Deck 7.

00:32:00.948 --> 00:32:02.040
We're losing life-support.

00:32:02.083 --> 00:32:03.380
Evacuate the deck.

00:32:03.417 --> 00:32:05.647
Tom, I need you at the conn.

00:32:07.655 --> 00:32:09.145
Aye, sir.

00:32:10.157 --> 00:32:11.749
Commander, they're arming

00:32:11.792 --> 00:32:13.692
their torpedo launchers
again.

00:32:13.728 --> 00:32:15.593
We cannot sustain
another direct hit.

00:32:15.629 --> 00:32:18.097
Kes, you seem to know
something about these weapons.

00:32:18.132 --> 00:32:19.531
Do you have any idea
how we can stop them?

00:32:19.567 --> 00:32:21.865
I'm not sure, but I think
it has something to do

00:32:21.902 --> 00:32:23.893
with remodulating
the targeting scanners.

00:32:23.938 --> 00:32:25.235
That could work.

00:32:25.272 --> 00:32:27.297
If we remodulate the scanners
to a parametric frequency,

00:32:27.341 --> 00:32:29.309
we might be able to destroy
the torpedo launchers

00:32:29.343 --> 00:32:30.571
before they fire.

00:32:30.611 --> 00:32:32.078
Mr. Tuvok, you heard the man.

00:32:32.113 --> 00:32:34.138
Tom, bring us about.

00:32:35.583 --> 00:32:36.777
Ready, Commander.

00:32:36.817 --> 00:32:38.648
Fire!

00:32:45.693 --> 00:32:47.627
Do you have a casualty report?

00:32:47.661 --> 00:32:50.994
Including Captain Janeway
and B'Elanna, we lost 11 people.

00:32:51.098 --> 00:32:52.929
What about the ship?

00:32:52.967 --> 00:32:55.527
Starboard shield generators
and warp drive are off-line,

00:32:55.569 --> 00:32:58.470
and power is down
on Decks 4 through 12.

00:32:58.506 --> 00:32:59.996
Make Deck 5 your priority.

00:33:00.040 --> 00:33:01.667
We've got to get
Sick Bay up and running again.

00:33:01.709 --> 00:33:02.869
Aye, sir.

00:33:02.910 --> 00:33:04.571
Kes, as far as what you say
is happening to you...

00:33:04.612 --> 00:33:06.705
I understand that my condition
can't be a priority now.

00:33:06.747 --> 00:33:08.942
Tom, I'm going to need you
to stay here

00:33:08.983 --> 00:33:10.575
and help treat these people.

00:33:10.618 --> 00:33:11.585
When this is over,

00:33:11.619 --> 00:33:13.883
we're all going to have
a lot of grieving to do.

00:33:15.489 --> 00:33:17.423
How are you doing?

00:33:18.759 --> 00:33:20.454
Tom?

00:33:20.494 --> 00:33:23.258
I know it doesn't
seem possible now,

00:33:23.297 --> 00:33:24.355
but you're going
to be all right.

00:33:24.398 --> 00:33:27.367
I wish I could believe you.

00:33:28.402 --> 00:33:29.528
You can.

00:33:32.840 --> 00:33:34.705
Thanks.

00:33:35.976 --> 00:33:38.376
Kes, we've got
radiation leakage

00:33:38.412 --> 00:33:40.141
coming from one of the Krenim
torpedo fragments.

00:33:40.181 --> 00:33:42.149
People are starting
to complain of nausea.

00:33:42.183 --> 00:33:44.947
Chroniton radiation.

00:33:46.921 --> 00:33:48.684
This is it.

00:33:48.722 --> 00:33:50.690
I'm infected.

00:33:50.724 --> 00:33:52.555
Where's the radiation
coming from?

00:33:52.593 --> 00:33:55.653
It's lodged in a Jefferies
tube on Deck 11, Section 2.

00:33:55.696 --> 00:33:57.357
I've got to get down there.

00:33:57.398 --> 00:33:58.990
You can't, the entire
deck is sealed off.

00:33:59.033 --> 00:34:00.694
I have to find the exact
temporal variance

00:34:00.734 --> 00:34:01.701
of that torpedo.

00:34:01.735 --> 00:34:02.929
You can't go near that thing.

00:34:03.003 --> 00:34:04.231
You'll be burned to a crisp.

00:34:04.271 --> 00:34:05.329
I know what I'm doing.

00:34:05.372 --> 00:34:06.361
You stay here and help Tom,
all right?

00:34:06.407 --> 00:34:07.738
Yes, but...

00:35:57.651 --> 00:35:58.982
Kes, how are you coming

00:35:59.086 --> 00:36:00.314
with those
analgesic compounds?

00:36:00.354 --> 00:36:02.379
Doctor, you've lost your hair.

00:36:02.423 --> 00:36:04.084
I beg your pardon?

00:36:04.124 --> 00:36:05.921
It's a long story.

00:36:05.993 --> 00:36:07.927
The important thing is,

00:36:08.028 --> 00:36:09.893
the temporal variance
of the chroniton torpedo

00:36:09.930 --> 00:36:12.296
was 1.47 microseconds.

00:36:23.577 --> 00:36:24.942
As far as I can determine,

00:36:25.012 --> 00:36:27.139
I've now jumped a total
of six years into my past.

00:36:27.181 --> 00:36:30.878
Do you have any theory
as to the cause of these jumps?

00:36:30.918 --> 00:36:33.113
According to Kes,
she and the rest of the crew

00:36:33.153 --> 00:36:35.144
will be infected
by chroniton radiation

00:36:35.189 --> 00:36:36.884
approximately 11 months
from now.

00:36:36.924 --> 00:36:38.084
Everyone will be inoculated

00:36:38.125 --> 00:36:39.786
and the effects
will appear to vanish.

00:36:39.827 --> 00:36:43.194
However, some five years later,
when I attempt an experimental...

00:36:43.230 --> 00:36:44.788
and I might add,
ingenious procedure

00:36:44.832 --> 00:36:47.232
to extend her life-span...
the bio-temporal field

00:36:47.267 --> 00:36:50.498
I expose her to will trigger
dormant chroniton particles,

00:36:50.537 --> 00:36:52.232
taking Kes out of temporal sync

00:36:52.272 --> 00:36:54.866
and causing her to begin her
backward journey through time.

00:36:54.908 --> 00:36:57.069
In all my years in Starfleet,

00:36:57.111 --> 00:37:00.774
I've never come across
a phenomenon quite like this.

00:37:00.814 --> 00:37:01.906
Kes has been able to provide us

00:37:02.016 --> 00:37:03.916
with the precise temporal
variance of the torpedo

00:37:03.951 --> 00:37:04.918
which infected her.

00:37:04.952 --> 00:37:07.250
Since Kes is moving
backward in time, she's

00:37:07.287 --> 00:37:08.914
already been infected
by the radiation poisoning.

00:37:09.023 --> 00:37:11.457
If we can set up
a bio-temporal chamber

00:37:11.492 --> 00:37:13.460
and expose her
to a precisely modulated field

00:37:13.494 --> 00:37:14.928
of antichroniton particles,

00:37:14.928 --> 00:37:16.361
of antichroniton particles,

00:37:16.396 --> 00:37:18.387
we feel this may purge
her system and bring her back

00:37:18.431 --> 00:37:20.228
into temporal sync
with the rest of us.

00:37:20.266 --> 00:37:21.927
Well, we better get moving.

00:37:22.035 --> 00:37:23.935
For all we know, Kes's
next jump will take her

00:37:23.970 --> 00:37:25.938
back to a time when
we're not here to help her.

00:37:26.005 --> 00:37:27.939
Captain, there's something else
I have to tell you.

00:37:28.041 --> 00:37:29.804
In about six months,
you're going to enter

00:37:29.842 --> 00:37:32.333
a region of space controlled
by a race called the Krenim.

00:37:32.378 --> 00:37:34.710
You must avoid them
at all costs.

00:37:34.747 --> 00:37:36.271
Tell me more.

00:37:36.316 --> 00:37:38.784
I'm ready to bring
the chamber on line.

00:37:38.818 --> 00:37:39.910
Synaptic relays are operational.

00:37:39.953 --> 00:37:41.284
How are her vital signs?

00:37:41.321 --> 00:37:43.949
Pulse normal,
body temperature 14 degrees.

00:37:44.057 --> 00:37:47.288
Chroniton level at 79 roentgens.

00:37:47.327 --> 00:37:50.990
Go ahead and activate
the chamber, Lieutenant.

00:37:53.866 --> 00:37:56.300
Increase the bio-temporal
field stress.

00:37:56.336 --> 00:37:59.464
Bringing field stress
to 25 kilodynes.

00:37:59.505 --> 00:38:02.599
All right, let's try
the antichronitons.

00:38:02.642 --> 00:38:05.406
Whenever you're ready, Doc.

00:38:08.581 --> 00:38:10.640
Initiating antichroniton burst.

00:38:10.683 --> 00:38:14.175
Ten MEVs, five second pulse.

00:38:18.257 --> 00:38:19.918
Pulse steady.

00:38:20.026 --> 00:38:23.154
Body temperature at 14.2 degrees
and rising.

00:38:23.196 --> 00:38:24.663
What about her chroniton count?

00:38:24.697 --> 00:38:27.029
Chroniton count...
is 71 roentgens

00:38:27.066 --> 00:38:28.624
and dropping.

00:38:28.668 --> 00:38:30.260
It's working.

00:38:30.303 --> 00:38:31.930
Lieutenant Torres,
increase the field

00:38:31.971 --> 00:38:33.598
strength to 30 kilodynes.

00:38:33.639 --> 00:38:34.606
Right.

00:38:34.640 --> 00:38:36.267
Initiating another burst.

00:38:36.309 --> 00:38:38.174
15 MEVs, five second pulse.

00:38:41.014 --> 00:38:43.380
Body temperature, 14.9 degrees.

00:38:43.416 --> 00:38:45.850
Chroniton count, 68 roentgens...

00:38:48.454 --> 00:38:49.443
sixty...

00:38:50.523 --> 00:38:51.717
fifty-seven...

00:38:53.493 --> 00:38:54.482
fifty-two...

00:38:57.497 --> 00:38:59.192
You need a cook.

00:38:59.232 --> 00:39:03.134
You haven't lived until
you've tasted my angla'bosque.

00:39:03.169 --> 00:39:05.865
It will be my job
to anticipate your needs

00:39:05.905 --> 00:39:07.600
before you know you have them.

00:39:07.640 --> 00:39:09.471
Not again.

00:39:09.509 --> 00:39:13.070
And I anticipate
your first need will be me.

00:39:13.112 --> 00:39:15.376
I'm sorry.

00:39:15.415 --> 00:39:17.815
I know this is going to
sound strange to you both,

00:39:17.850 --> 00:39:19.408
but I don't belong here.

00:39:19.452 --> 00:39:21.511
But we discussed this.

00:39:21.554 --> 00:39:23.886
You don't understand.

00:39:23.923 --> 00:39:26.289
I'm traveling backwards
in time, getting younger.

00:39:26.325 --> 00:39:29.351
We have to lower
my chroniton levels.

00:39:29.395 --> 00:39:30.362
You've got to get me

00:39:30.396 --> 00:39:31.920
into the bio-temporal
chamber right away.

00:39:31.998 --> 00:39:33.522
I-I'm sorry, Captain.

00:39:33.566 --> 00:39:36.228
I-I didn't quite
anticipate this.

00:39:36.269 --> 00:39:37.759
Listen to me, please.

00:39:37.804 --> 00:39:39.499
Sweeting, try to calm down.

00:39:39.539 --> 00:39:40.597
I assure you, Captain,

00:39:40.640 --> 00:39:41.937
she's never behaved
this way before.

00:39:42.041 --> 00:39:43.941
Hold on a minute, Mr. Neelix.

00:39:44.043 --> 00:39:46.375
Kes, why don't you start over
slowly?

00:39:46.412 --> 00:39:49.279
It begins about eight years
in the future

00:39:49.315 --> 00:39:51.146
when I'm about to die...

00:39:51.184 --> 00:39:52.583
No!

00:40:00.259 --> 00:40:01.317
Time for dinner.

00:40:04.230 --> 00:40:05.959
What's wrong, Kes?

00:40:13.506 --> 00:40:14.871
Who are you?

00:40:14.907 --> 00:40:16.966
What is this place?

00:40:17.009 --> 00:40:18.135
We don't have time to play

00:40:18.177 --> 00:40:19.701
our guessing game
right now, Kes.

00:40:19.745 --> 00:40:21.736
You know how your mother gets
when we're late to the table.

00:40:21.781 --> 00:40:24.147
You're my father.

00:40:24.183 --> 00:40:27.311
That's right, and you're
my favorite daughter,

00:40:27.353 --> 00:40:28.342
but don't tell anyone.

00:40:28.387 --> 00:40:29.615
Listen to me.

00:40:29.655 --> 00:40:31.247
Something terrible's
been happening to me.

00:40:31.290 --> 00:40:33.121
What's wrong?

00:40:33.159 --> 00:40:34.126
There might not be much time,

00:40:34.160 --> 00:40:35.388
so I've got to explain
this quickly.

00:40:35.428 --> 00:40:37.328
Please try to believe me.

00:40:37.363 --> 00:40:38.990
I've been living aboard
a starship called Voyager.

00:40:39.065 --> 00:40:42.000
A starship... I see.

00:40:42.068 --> 00:40:44.628
So now it's not only the surface
you're dreaming about exploring.

00:40:44.670 --> 00:40:45.637
Listen to me.

00:40:45.671 --> 00:40:47.104
I did go to the surface,

00:40:47.140 --> 00:40:48.801
or, rather, I will go there,

00:40:48.841 --> 00:40:49.967
and the people aboard the ship,

00:40:50.009 --> 00:40:51.533
they're going to rescue me
from the Kazon

00:40:51.577 --> 00:40:52.771
and take me with them.

00:40:52.812 --> 00:40:53.870
Why don't you finish telling me

00:40:53.913 --> 00:40:55.141
about your adventures
after dinner?

00:40:55.181 --> 00:40:56.239
No! There's no time.

00:40:56.282 --> 00:40:57.681
You've got to believe me.

00:40:57.717 --> 00:40:58.877
One moment, I was
this old woman,

00:40:58.918 --> 00:41:00.215
and then, and then...

00:41:00.253 --> 00:41:01.550
Kes, we're late.

00:41:01.587 --> 00:41:03.020
Father, please.

00:41:07.059 --> 00:41:08.492
I can see the toes!

00:41:08.528 --> 00:41:09.893
It's coming, Martis.

00:41:18.371 --> 00:41:19.633
It's a girl!

00:41:20.673 --> 00:41:22.072
Oh!

00:41:22.108 --> 00:41:25.134
Oh, Kes!

00:41:25.178 --> 00:41:26.509
Oh!

00:41:26.546 --> 00:41:28.639
Oh...

00:42:03.149 --> 00:42:05.014
It's a girl!

00:42:06.118 --> 00:42:07.346
Oh!

00:42:07.386 --> 00:42:09.115
Oh, she's so...

00:42:09.155 --> 00:42:10.884
she's so beautiful.

00:42:10.923 --> 00:42:12.288
Kes!

00:42:12.325 --> 00:42:15.726
Oh...

00:42:17.296 --> 00:42:21.130
I think one day,
she'll see the sun.

00:42:30.176 --> 00:42:31.939
51 roentgens.

00:42:31.978 --> 00:42:34.446
Forty-six...

00:42:34.480 --> 00:42:36.641
thirty-four.

00:42:36.682 --> 00:42:38.912
Another antichroniton burst...
20 MEVs.

00:42:38.951 --> 00:42:40.816
Right.

00:42:40.853 --> 00:42:43.321
Levels are continuing to drop.

00:42:43.356 --> 00:42:44.516
Pulse normal.

00:42:44.557 --> 00:42:48.391
Body temperature steady
at 16.3 degrees.

00:42:49.462 --> 00:42:52.898
Chroniton levels
are at zero roentgens.

00:42:53.866 --> 00:42:55.834
Welcome back, Kes.

00:42:55.868 --> 00:42:57.460
What's the date?

00:42:57.503 --> 00:42:58.800
How old am I?

00:42:58.838 --> 00:42:59.862
The same age you were

00:42:59.905 --> 00:43:01.770
when we put you into
the bio-temporal chamber...

00:43:01.807 --> 00:43:04.776
a healthy three years
and two months.

00:43:04.810 --> 00:43:07.574
And due to an extraordinary
display of medical heroics,

00:43:07.613 --> 00:43:09.911
you're back in temporal sync
with the rest of us.

00:43:17.556 --> 00:43:21.083
So, I'm going to become
a security officer.

00:43:21.127 --> 00:43:22.594
How about that?

00:43:22.628 --> 00:43:25.620
Fortunately, Mr. Neelix,
what Kes has been describing

00:43:25.665 --> 00:43:27.462
is merely one possible future.

00:43:27.500 --> 00:43:29.297
On each occasion that she jumped

00:43:29.335 --> 00:43:31.963
to a previous time,
her subsequent actions

00:43:32.071 --> 00:43:34.699
most likely altered the future
from that moment on.

00:43:34.740 --> 00:43:36.708
Good point, Tuvok.

00:43:36.742 --> 00:43:39.540
Maybe I'll turn out to be
Chief Security Officer.

00:43:39.578 --> 00:43:41.307
So, Kes...

00:43:41.347 --> 00:43:43.975
have you regained all
your memories of the past?

00:43:44.083 --> 00:43:47.177
I remember last month's
supply of replicator rations

00:43:47.219 --> 00:43:49.983
that you borrowed
that you owe me...

00:43:50.056 --> 00:43:51.489
if that's what you're asking.

00:43:51.524 --> 00:43:53.822
Don't worry.
I haven't forgotten.

00:43:53.859 --> 00:43:55.486
I realize
it's only hypothetical,

00:43:55.528 --> 00:43:57.086
but still,
I'd be curious to know

00:43:57.129 --> 00:43:58.858
what sorts
of medical breakthroughs

00:43:58.898 --> 00:44:01.162
I'm going to make
in this possible future.

00:44:01.200 --> 00:44:02.667
It's not as if I've
seen everything

00:44:02.702 --> 00:44:04.761
that's going to happen
over the next six years.

00:44:04.804 --> 00:44:07.830
I only remember short periods
I experienced between jumps.

00:44:07.873 --> 00:44:10.933
Even so, I bet you found out
some pretty interesting things.

00:44:10.976 --> 00:44:13.171
Yeah, Kes.
Tell us what you know.

00:44:13.212 --> 00:44:14.270
Careful, Tom.

00:44:14.313 --> 00:44:15.678
You may find out
that you leave Voyager

00:44:15.715 --> 00:44:17.307
only to join a monastery.

00:44:17.350 --> 00:44:19.648
Hey, give him a little credit.

00:44:19.685 --> 00:44:21.277
I'll bet he gets married
and has a family.

00:44:21.320 --> 00:44:22.287
Thank you.

00:44:22.321 --> 00:44:23.288
Don't mention it.

00:44:23.322 --> 00:44:24.414
Are you telling?

00:44:24.457 --> 00:44:25.856
Well...

00:44:25.891 --> 00:44:26.915
as Tuvok said,

00:44:26.959 --> 00:44:28.950
I've only seen pieces
of one possible future.

00:44:29.028 --> 00:44:29.960
You know what?

00:44:30.029 --> 00:44:31.587
Don't tell me.
I don't want to know.

00:44:31.630 --> 00:44:33.291
I like a little
mystery in my life.

00:44:33.332 --> 00:44:34.560
Tom's right.

00:44:34.600 --> 00:44:37.865
I think we should all leave
the future to the future.

00:44:37.903 --> 00:44:39.962
While I agree it would
not be wise for Kes

00:44:40.039 --> 00:44:41.939
to make all of her
experiences public,

00:44:41.974 --> 00:44:43.407
a report on anything she knows

00:44:43.442 --> 00:44:45.205
about these Krenim
might be useful.

00:44:45.244 --> 00:44:47.144
I'll get started right away.

00:44:47.179 --> 00:44:48.373
Hang on a minute.

00:44:48.414 --> 00:44:49.381
I didn't mean now.

00:44:49.415 --> 00:44:50.780
Stay and enjoy your party.

00:44:50.816 --> 00:44:52.215
If there's one thing
that this experience

00:44:52.251 --> 00:44:53.309
has taught me, Captain,

00:44:53.352 --> 00:44:55.343
it's that there's no
time like the present.
